<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user}>
  <article class="space-y-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-base-content/75">
      Remote Retro collects only what it needs to run your retrospectives.
    </p>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">What we store</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-base-content/75">
        <li>
          Your Google profile basics: name, email address and profile picture, received when you sign in.
          We also store whether Google verified that email, and the Google Workspace domain when
          Google sends one, so AI features can be limited to an organization.
        </li>
        <li>
          The retros you take part in and what you add to them: ideas, groups, labels, votes and action items.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">How it's used</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-base-content/75">
        <li>To sign you in and show who's taking part in a retro.</li>
        <li>To let other participants of a retro see its content.</li>
        <li>
          If AI assistance is enabled, the text of a retro's ideas is sent to Google's Gemini
          (Vertex AI) to suggest groups. It isn't used for anything else.
        </li>
        <li>
          When a retro is closed, each participant is emailed its action items. We don't send
          any other email.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">What we don't do</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-base-content/75">
        <li>No advertising, analytics or third-party tracking scripts.</li>
        <li>No marketing email. We don't send email at all.</li>
        <li>We never sell or share your data.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Cookies</h2>
      <p class="text-base-content/75">
        A single session cookie keeps you signed in. Your light/dark theme choice is kept in your browser's local storage.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layouts.app>
